+/*
+ * LINUX64 (xnulinux): hosted, idle goes straight to the host, which runs Linux until XNU's next timer deadline and
+ * comes back; the due timer is then delivered here as its interrupt would be. No WFE/WFI and no timer interrupt of
+ * XNU's own apply (idle_enable stays FALSE without the CPU kext: cpu_machine_init never runs).
